---
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About | Daniele Sala"
	description="Environmental engineer specialised in hydrology and climate risk analytics. M.Sc. Politecnico di Milano 106/110. Based in Milan, working across Europe."
>
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="About"
				tagline="Environmental engineer specialised in hydrology, flood risk modeling and climate risk analytics."
			/>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Background</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						In September 2025, the Seveso and Bevera rivers overflowed across Northern Lombardy. I
						was on the operational team running the hydrological alerts, post-event impact assessment
						and institutional reporting that fed directly into Regione Lombardia's emergency
						declarations. That kind of work, where hydrological models meet real consequences for
						real cities, is exactly what I do as a freelancer too: flood risk modeling, climate data
						analytics and CSRD-aligned physical risk for engineering firms, insurers and climate-tech
						teams across Europe.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Experience</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<h3>Natural Risk Assessment Specialist, Progesi S.p.A.</h3>
					<p class="role-period">2025 – Present</p>
					<p>
						Designed and operated environmental monitoring and hydrological forecasting workflows
						powered by ICON and ECMWF numerical weather prediction models. Built decision-support
						dashboards in Python, R and MATLAB to translate raw forecast data into actionable risk
						signals for institutional stakeholders.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>September 2025 flood event (Seveso &amp; Bevera rivers):</strong> Led
						end-to-end flood risk management workflow from hydrological alerting and real-time monitoring
						to post-event impact assessment and institutional reporting, supporting municipalities and
						Regione Lombardia in emergency state declarations and public infrastructure damage compensation
						claims.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Skills demonstrated:</strong> hydrological forecasting · NWP data pipelines (ICON,
						ECMWF-IFS) · real-time monitoring · Python/R/MATLAB dashboarding · operational decision
						support under uncertainty · institutional reporting.
					</p>
					<p>
						<em
							>Specific deliverables and client outputs remain confidential under NDA. Methodology
							available for discussion under mutual NDA.</em
						>
					</p>

					<h3>Climate Data Analyst, Enel S.p.A.</h3>
					<p class="role-period">2024</p>
					<p>
						Developed climate-risk analytics aligned with the EU Corporate Sustainability Reporting
						Directive (CSRD) for a global energy infrastructure portfolio. Translated physical and
						transition climate risks into quantitative metrics consumable by sustainability and finance
						teams. Built Python/R automation for recurring climate data ingestion and cross-indicator
						sustainability benchmarking.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Skills demonstrated:</strong> CSRD-aligned climate risk methodology · physical risk
						modeling for energy assets · climate scenario analysis · ESG reporting workflows · global
						portfolio analytics.
					</p>
					<p>
						<em>All client data, portfolio specifics and output metrics confidential under NDA.</em>
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Education</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<h3>M.Sc. Environmental and Land Planning Engineering</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Politecnico di Milano · 2021–2024</p>
					<p>Core coursework: Hydrogeological Risk, Remote Sensing, Statistical Models and Stochastic Processes</p>

					<h3>Erasmus Exchange</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Universitat Politècnica de València, Spain · 2022–2023</p>
					<p>Specialization: Water Quality, Pollution Transport, Wastewater Treatment</p>

					<h3>B.Sc. Environmental Engineering</h3>
					<p class="role-period">Politecnico di Milano · 2018–2021</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Certifications &amp; Languages</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>ENAC A1/A3 UAS Operator Certificate (Open Category)</p>
					<p>Italian (native) · English (C1) · Spanish (B2)</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.content :global(h3) {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--gray-0);
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.content :global(h3:first-child) {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.role-period {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-400);
		margin-top: -0.5rem;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 60% 1fr;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}
	}
</style>
